more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
[Intro - Dripping water AND VALLEY MIST makes a resonant arpeggio over a bass drone with cathedral reverberation]  
  
[Verse 1 - trancelike Earthy and warm contralto UK female voice]  
(A single blade)  
(Of Grass)  
  
[Verse 2 - dreamy reverie as the grass basks in the suns rays. UK Female vocals, mezzo soprano]  
Sunlight caresses a blade of green,    
Chlorophyll awakens in nature serene.    
Within the core, magnesium bound,    
Life unfolds, can you hear the sound?    
Photons dance, a vibrant song,    
Carbohydrates make me strong.   
A blade of grass, and round we go,    
Fuel for life, with the sun's warm glow.      
  
[Chorus - chanting choir with harmony and reverb]  
Photosynthesis, a wondrous play,    
In light we thrive, come what may.    
Green leaves whisper ancient tales,    
Where life renews, and never fails.    
Cycles turning, ever bright,    
In the sun's embrace, a guiding light.    
Photosynthesis, nature’s plant,    
A dance of life we all must chant.   
  
[Verse 3 - the grass sings with increasing vitality and excitement. UK female contralto voice]  
I welcome the light with fervent delight,    
Rejoicing in gases fixed from the sky's height.    
Eagah beneath these vast blue skies, my dreams ignite,    
Breathing in energy, so pure and bright.    
With every breeze, whispers of life,    
Soil and water make me thrive.    
A living thread in nature's grand design,    
Sustained by sun, air, and time.  
  
[Bridge - foreboding. Irish Female contralto vocal]  
A sense of presence in the air,    
Footsteps slow, yet drawing near.    
The grazing beast, a soft shadow cast,    
Soon to partake in its humble repast.    
In harmony we exist, matter intertwined,    
A moment in this cycle we find.    
The grass wonders in gentle reflection,    
Embracing its role in life's intersection.  
  
[Verse 4 - stoic swirling dissolution, contralto female voice in major key]  
In the lush meadow, a transformation flows,    
Where grass becomes life, as time bestows.    
The grazing cow with every breath,    
Turns the blade to strength amidst death.    
A modern dance, in the present's glow,    
Essences blend, in nature's show.    
A union of life, cow and calf,    
In today's rumen, where futures craft.    
Together they become, life's warm embrace,    
In the balance of nature, a shared grace.  
  
[Chorus -  chanting choir with harmonies and reverb]  
A dance of time, I stride so grand,    
In sunlight's glow, I make my stand.    
My ancient call echoes through the land,    
Where life thrives, and cycles expand.    
Moments passing, ever free,    
In the sun's embrace, I roam with glee.    
A dance of life, a prehistoric trance,    
Through ages past in nature's dance.   
  
[Verse 5]  
(A single blade)  
(Of Grass)  
  
--more    
